<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB leaves discount rate unchanged.</title>
<headline>SNB leaves discount rate unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank said it left its discount rate unchanged at 1.00 percent after a regular weekly meeting of its central bank council.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been no change,&quot; an SNB spokesman said.</p>
<p>The rate has been kept at 1.00 percent since it was lowered from 1.50 percent on September 26.</p>
<p>The rate at current levels matches the historic low maintained from February 1978 to November 1979. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
